      <h3>What is the best code right now</h3>
      <p><strong>ADAMANDLINDS</strong>: 10% off any Ubigi plan. It's our own code, shown first; other working codes give the same 10%.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>What's the difference between a one-off and a recurring Ubigi plan</h3>
      <p>A one-off plan is a fixed data allowance valid for a set number of days, bought once. A recurring plan renews automatically: monthly (charged and refreshed every month, cancellable only after a 3-month minimum) or annual (paid in full upfront for 12 months of monthly refreshes, non-cancellable and non-refundable during that year).</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Can I cancel a recurring Ubigi plan</h3>
      <p>A monthly plan, yes, but not until you've held it for at least 3 months. An annual plan cannot be cancelled or refunded during its 12-month term.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Does unused Ubigi data roll over</h3>
      <p>No. Whatever you don't use in a billing period is gone, whether you're on a one-off, monthly, or annual plan.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Who actually runs Ubigi</h3>
      <p>Transatel, a French MVNO enabler in operation since the early 2000s and now part of NTT Group. Transatel also supplies the connectivity behind connected-car systems for BMW, Toyota, Jeep, Maserati, Fiat, Alfa Romeo, Mini, Jaguar, and Land Rover.</p>
